<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <!-- Compiler settings shared by the engine libraries, csyren_host, the engine tests and
       project executables (through CSyren.project.props). Import after Microsoft.Cpp.props.
       Third-party projects (imGui, Jolt) do not import it.

       cstdmf/window_clean.h is force-included first in every translation unit: <Windows.h>
       is always included once, lean (WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN + NOMINMAX), and its near/far
       macros are removed before any engine header is parsed (core::Camera::near/far).
       The compiler and IntelliSense then see the same macro set in every file, whatever
       the include order or the translation unit a header is parsed in.

       The engine builds without RTTI (/GR-): types are identified with core::TypeKey
       and core::typeName (lib/core/type_key.h), and tools/csyren_registry.py fails the
       build on typeid / type_info / type_index / dynamic_cast / std::any in engine code.
       A project that needs RTTI (the tests: googletest is prebuilt with it) sets
       <CSyrenRuntimeTypeInfo>true</CSyrenRuntimeTypeInfo>.

       /utf-8: sources are UTF-8 (without a BOM; .editorconfig sets it for new files) and
       are compiled as UTF-8, string literals included. Without it cl reads a file without
       a BOM in the system code page, while IntelliSense reads it as UTF-8: a Windows-1251
       comment then breaks every IntelliSense parse that includes the file, standard
       headers included, although the build is clean. tools/tests/test_source_encoding.py
       rejects sources that are not UTF-8. -->
  <ItemDefinitionGroup>
    <ClCompile>
      <RuntimeTypeInfo Condition="'$(CSyrenRuntimeTypeInfo)'!='true'">false</RuntimeTypeInfo>
      <ForcedIncludeFiles>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)lib\cstdmf\window_clean.h;%(ForcedIncludeFiles)</ForcedIncludeFiles>
      <PreprocessorDefinitions>NOMINMAX;%(PreprocessorDefinitions)</PreprocessorDefinitions>
      <AdditionalOptions>/utf-8 %(AdditionalOptions)</AdditionalOptions>
    </ClCompile>
  </ItemDefinitionGroup>
</Project>
